# S1/S7/S9 licence-free leg - enable the CPU web server and one Web API user in
# the bench's station project (Part IV s.11.1a). Offline: nothing here touches the
# controller; download_1214c.plan (--set um=reset the first time) carries it to the CPU.
#
#   set FRAKTAL_TIA_WEB_PASSWORD=<the web user's password>   (never in a plan or log)
#   Fraktal.Tia.Cli plan webapi_1214c.plan --set work=%LOCALAPPDATA%\Fraktal\TiaStations
#
# Why the Web API: JSON-RPC over HTTPS is built into every S7-1500 and every
# S7-1200 from V4.5, needs no runtime licence (the OPC UA server needs one per
# CPU), and reads optimized data symbolically. It honours the same "Accessible /
# Writable from HMI/OPC UA/Web API" member attributes the generator already sets.
#
# Measured on the 1214C V4.7.3 / TIA V20 (2026-10-08):
#  - WebserverActivate is the only listed web-server switch; WebserverHttpsOnly and
#    the interface's UseWebServerForInterface are not supported on this family.
#  - HTTPS needs a certificate AND a certificate type. The type is TIA's internal
#    WebserverCertificateType (0 NoneSelected, 1 HardwareGenerated, 2
#    SoftwareDownloaded); Openness V20 knows the name but supports neither its
#    getter nor its setter on a 1214C. It is therefore ONE MANUAL STEP per station
#    in the TIA editor (PLC_1 > Properties > Web server > Security: certificate
#    loaded via the software, server certificate PLC-1/Webserver-<n>), kept in the
#    station project. Until it is set the hardware compile reports "No certificate
#    type is assigned to the Web server security" and a download refuses.
#  - There is no classic web-user list: web users are UMAC project users, so access
#    control is enabled "via access level". Then access without login (the
#    anonymous user) must be full access or a full-access password must be set.
#    BENCH: anonymous gets the PLCAdministrator system role (the three access
#    levels, no web/OPC UA rights) = today's "full access, no password" posture.
#    A deployed station sets the full-access password instead (Part IV s.14).
open-project --path ${work}\FrkSpikeS2\FrkSpikeS2.ap20
service-set --plc PLC_1 --service PlcAccessControlConfigurationProvider --prop PlcAccessControlConfiguration --value EnabledWithAccessControlViaAccessLevel
set-hw-attribute --plc PLC_1 --attr WebserverActivate --value true
# created once, then kept (clients pin its fingerprint)
webserver-certificate --plc PLC_1
# kept as tolerant probes: they record whether a later Openness exposes the setter
? set-hw-attribute --plc PLC_1 --attr WebserverCertificateType --value 2 --type int
umac-user --plc PLC_1 --anonymous --system-roles PLCAdministrator
# least privilege: the gateway user reads and writes process data, nothing else (no
# operating-mode change, diagnostics, firmware, files, backup) - which HMI user may
# command is the gateway's Core s.14 role mapping, as on AB
umac-user --plc PLC_1 --name fraktal --password-env FRAKTAL_TIA_WEB_PASSWORD --role FraktalGateway --rights WebReadTags,WebWriteTags
umac-user --plc PLC_1 --list
hw-attributes --plc PLC_1 --filter Web
# tolerant only for the manual certificate-type step above; download compiles
# again and refuses on any error
? compile --plc PLC_1 --hw
save
